In article <B532D81B@ocr.com>, STEVE.MEIROWSKY@ocr.com (steve meirowsky) writes...
>I sure would appreciate someone adding a feature to NetHacke that would
>allow a player a maximum amount of time to play.  If they were still
>playing after the time ran out, it would automatically save the game and
>kick them out...  Thanks in advance!

I think this would only be useful on a multiuser system, not on a PC.
But on a multiuser system with U*X or VMS, it should be possible to achieve
this by system functions.
For example, I once knew a U*X host where the /usr/games directory
was open only during the lunch-break. (Just some crontab entries, I think)
Kicking off someone who plays too long could possibly also be done by some 
accounting software.
Therefore, there is no need to implement such a feature. 


